# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-11-09 blanket rules.
#
# The per-scan lists above kept drifting out of date: every new scan added
# another filename and a few always slipped through. Scraped payloads are now
# excluded by shape instead of by name, so a new scan is ignored by default and
# has to be opted in explicitly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Root-level JSON is always a scrape or a run artifact. The two config files
# that do belong in git are re-included by name.
/*.json
!/products.example.json
!/railway.json

# Same for the other raw-payload shapes that land in the repo root.
/*.csv
/*.html
/*.pdf
/*.xml
/*.png
/*.ndjson

# Run workspaces. These hold raw evidence JSON, profile screenshots of real
# people, vendored third-party checkouts (each with its own .git), and rendered
# report HTML — 270MB+ that belongs on disk, not in history. The reports
# themselves ship via Feishu/Obsidian; only the tooling is versioned here.
/outputs/
/reports/
/sites/
/out-h3ig/
/out-h3promo/

# macOS noise, editor leftovers, in-place script backups
.DS_Store
*.bak
*.esc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-11-10, going public. Everything below runs locally and stays local.
#
# Same policy as the "Internal GTM tooling" block above, applied to the Sep-Nov
# 2026 campaign scripts and their write-ups. Three separate reasons:
#
#   1. Private correspondence and commercial terms, including verbatim DM
#      threads with named individuals and per-post payment offers. None of
#      those people agreed to be published.
#   2. Client product plans, and targeting lists of real people built around
#      them.
#   3. Client-internal documents and the workspace tokens that address them.
#
# The generic radar, the outreach pipeline, and the public-data scan scripts
# are unaffected — that is what this repository publishes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Report write-ups: every root-level markdown except this project's own README.
/*.md
!/README.md

# Campaign one-offs built around client product plans and named individuals
tools/pro_influencer_*.py
tools/core_kol_*.py
tools/outreach_status_push_20261020.py

# Queries derived from a client-internal evaluation
tools/spacebunny_dimension_scan.py

# Writers that embed Feishu Base / Sheet tokens for internal workspaces
tools/campaign_push_feishu_20261019.py
tools/close_mutuals_table_20261019.py
tools/close_mutuals_table_T117_20261019.py
tools/flash_kol_push_feishu_20260922.py
